Track 2: Orion’s Eyebrow Twitches
- Story & Context: Mara sits on the rooftop, squinting through a lens that has been cracked since the accelerator riot, mapping the stars not by name but by the way their light stutters against the suburban sky. She hums along to the mechanical grinding of the neighbors' satellite dish, remembering how the Accelerator scene forced her to choose between the gravity of the Earth and the pull of the vacuum. "I watch the constellations fail to blink," she whispers into the cold air, feeling the familiar, nauseating vertigo of a shifting orbit.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A hyper-realistic, desaturated close-up of a cracked telescope lens showing a blurry, smeared image of a constellation, moody, melancholy, night-sky atmosphere.

Track 3: 0.004 Kelvin Flux
- Story & Context: Legend says the night the accelerator finally went dark, the remaining members of the Collective performed a requiem that cooled the center of the ring to a near-absolute zero, freezing the soundwaves in mid-air. Locals still claim that if you stand in the center of the ruin, you can see the ghosts of the heat-maps flickering in the shadows of the floorboards, a haunting trace of the night the music became physical. "Nothing moves once the heat stops bleeding," is the final phrase etched into the steel casing of the main console, serving as the epitaph for the loudest night in physics history.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A cinematic, ethereal shot of a frozen, crystalline circuit board hovering in mid-air inside a cavernous, dark industrial hall, illuminated by faint, freezing blue starlight.

